Vamos prosseguir com a traducao do hino 13:

13 - Great is Thy faithfulness
referencias biblicas do hino: Lam 3:22-23 - Jam 1:17 - Psa 36:5; 89:1 

1. Great is Thy faithfulness, O God, my Father;
There is no shadow of turning with Thee.
Thou changest not, Thy compassions, they fail not;
As Thou hast been, Thou forever will be.

    Refrain:
    Great is Thy faithfulness! Great is Thy faithfulness!
    Morning by morning new mercies I see;
    All I have needed, Thy hand hath provided;
    Great is Thy faithfulness, Lord, unto me!

2. Seasons change every year, winter to summer;
Spring flowers blossom, and harvests we reap.
Sun, moon and stars in the skies still shine brightly;
All show Thy faithfulness to us runs deep.

3. Pardon for sin and a peace that endureth,
Thine own dear presence to lead and to guide;
Strength for today and bright hope for tomorrow,
All of these blessings, Lord, Thou dost provide.


A partitura eh 3/4 em E bemol Maior, velocidade 100 seminimas

As notas sao:
Notas para as estrofes 1, 2 e 3:
verset 1: sm sm sm sm. c sm sm sm sm sm m
verset 2: sm sm sm sm. c sm sm sm sm m.
verset 3: sm sm sm sm. c sm sm sm sm sm m
verset 4: sm sm sm sm. c sm sm sm sm m.

refrain:
verset 1: sm sm sm c. sc m sm sm sm c. sc m
verset 2: sm sm sm sm sm sm sm sm sm m.
verset 3: sm sm sm sm. c sm sm sm sm sm m
verset 4: sm sm sm sm. c sm(fermata)' sm sm sm m.

legenda: 
sb = semibreve
m = minima
sm = seminima
c = colcheia
sc = semicolcheia
m. = minima pontuada
sm. = seminima pontuada
c. = colcheia pontuada
m_sm* = minima ligada a uma seminima = 1 som
sm(fermata)' = seminima com uma fermata (som deve ser sustentado = 1 silaba), seguida de uma respiracao (pausa)

